ecials":{"text":"<a href=\"https://www.dijaedadula.com/blog\" style=\"color:rgba(26,26,26,1);text-decoration:none\">Blog</a>"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":15,"fontWeight":"500","height":24,"left":414,"lineHeight":"1.4","textAlign":"center","top":26,"width":110}},"mobile":{"config":{"hide":true},"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":14,"height":22,"left":270,"lineHeight":"1.4","textAlign":"center","top":22,"width":130}}}},{"id":"l_2107","type":"line","responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"borderColor":"rgba(230,232,236,1)","left":0,"top":63,"width":960}},"mobile":{"styles":{"borderColor":"rgba(230,232,236,1)","left":0,"top":60,"width":420}}}}]},{"id":"sec_2108","type":"section","responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","height":8642}},"mobile":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","height":11219}}},"children":[{"id":"t_2109","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"<a href=\"https://www.dijaedadula.com/blog\" style=\"color:rgba(0,122,102,1);text-decoration:underline\">Blog</a> · CRM and automation that sells"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"400","height":25,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":64,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":13,"fontWeight":"400","height":24,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":48,"width":380}}}},{"id":"t_2110","type":"text-block","specials":{"tag":"h1","text":"AI Agents for Real Estate: Qualify Leads, Book Viewings and Follow Up"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":42,"fontWeight":"800","height":154,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.18","textAlign":"left","top":105,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":30,"fontWeight":"800","height":112,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.18","textAlign":"left","top":84,"width":380}}}},{"id":"t_2111","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"What an AI agent should do for a real estate business, the four questions that qualify a buyer, how it books viewings, and what must stay with a licensed agent."},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(85,85,85,1)","fontSize":21,"fontWeight":"400","height":98,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":277,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(85,85,85,1)","fontSize":18,"fontWeight":"400","height":112,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":210,"width":380}}}},{"id":"t_2112","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"By <a href=\"https://www.dijaedadula.com/home\" style=\"color:rgba(0,122,102,1);text-decoration:underline\">Dijae Dadula</a> · November 6, 2026 · 8 min read"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"400","height":25,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":393,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":13,"fontWeight":"400","height":24,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":336,"width":380}}}},{"id":"eb_2120","type":"editor-blog","specials":{"html":"<div class='dd-article dd-c'>\n<figure class='dd-fig'><div class='dd-shot' style='aspect-ratio:16/9'><img src='https://statics.pancake.vn/web-media-264/c7/de/14/9c/5bb4c6948b208261758f7834edac318ba4e7b83aa680e2b710c3e832.png' alt='Paper-cut illustration at night of a phone with a chat bubble, a dotted path leading past a calendar with a check mark and a house key to the door of a house beside a condo tower' width='1536' height='864' loading='lazy'></div></figure>\n<div class='dd-scene'><span class='dd-note-label'>Picture this · illustrative</span>\n<p>It is 10:40 on a Saturday night. Someone sees your listing for a two-bedroom condo and sends a message: “Is this still available? Can I see it this week?” Your agents are asleep. By Sunday noon, when someone finally replies, the buyer has already booked a viewing with another listing that answered in two minutes.</p></div>\n<p class='dd-plain'>An AI agent for real estate is <mark>a first responder that answers listing questions, qualifies the buyer and books the viewing, then hands the lead to a licensed agent.</mark></p>\n<div class='dd-words'><span><b>Lead</b> anyone who asks about a property</span><span><b>Qualify</b> learn if, what and when they will buy</span><span><b>Viewing</b> a booked property visit</span><span><b>Handoff</b> a licensed agent takes over</span><span><b>Nurture</b> follow-up for buyers who are not ready yet</span></div>\n<nav class='dd-toc' aria-label='Table of contents'>\n<p class='dd-toc-title'>Questions in this guide</p>\n<ol>\n<li><a href='#what'>What can an AI agent do for real estate?</a></li>\n<li><a href='#qualify'>Which questions qualify a buyer?</a></li>\n<li><a href='#speed'>How fast should a lead get a reply?</a></li>\n<li><a href='#viewings'>How does it book viewings?</a></li>\n<li><a href='#limits'>What must stay with a licensed agent?</a></li>\n<li><a href='#try'>What can you set up today?</a></li>\n</ol>\n</nav>\n<h2 id='what'>What can an AI agent actually do for a real estate business?</h2>\n<p class='dd-short'><b>Short answer:</b> the repetitive first steps. It answers listing questions, asks a few qualifying questions, books viewings, sends reminders and keeps following up, so your agents spend their time with serious buyers.</p>\n<p>Most real estate inquiries ask the same things: is it still available, how much, where exactly, can I see it, what are the payment terms. An AI agent grounded in your current listings answers these in seconds, on Messenger, Instagram, WhatsApp or your website. It does not replace the agent. Buyers still want a person: in the National Association of REALTORS® 2025 Profile of Home Buyers and Sellers, 88% of US buyers purchased through an agent or broker.</p>\n<div class='dd-table-wrap'><table>\n<thead><tr><th>The AI agent handles</th><th>A licensed agent handles</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Availability, price, location and amenities from your listing data</td><td>Advice on value, offers and negotiation</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Three or four qualifying questions</td><td>Reading the buyer's needs on a call or a viewing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Booking, confirming and rescheduling viewings</td><td>Running the viewing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Reminders and patient follow-up</td><td>Paperwork, financing guidance and closing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Tagging and routing the lead in your CRM</td><td>Any complaint, sensitive question or exception</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<figure class='dd-fig'>\n<svg viewBox='0 0 640 260' role='img' aria-labelledby='sc1t sc1d' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'>\n<title id='sc1t'>A real estate lead's journey, sketched</title>\n<desc id='sc1d'>A dashed path runs from a chat bubble on the left through three stops, answer, qualify and book viewing, to a house on the right, where a licensed agent takes over. A highlighted note says the AI opens the door and the agent walks them through it.</desc>\n<defs><pattern id='sc1g' width='16' height='16' patternUnits='userSpaceOnUse'><circle cx='2' cy='2' r='1' fill='#e6dccb'/></pattern></defs>\n<rect x='0' y='0' width='640' height='260' rx='14' fill='#fbf7f0'/>\n<rect x='0' y='0' width='640' height='260' rx='14' fill='url(#sc1g)'/>\n<path d='M92 170 C 150 100, 190 100, 220 120 S 300 200, 350 170 S 430 90, 470 110 S 520 170, 548 160' fill='none' stroke='#007a66' stroke-width='3' stroke-dasharray='8 7' stroke-linecap='round'/>\n<rect x='24' y='146' width='72' height='46' rx='18' fill='#fff' stroke='#007a66' stroke-width='2.5'/><text x='36' y='175' class='svg-t'>Hi!</text>\n<text x='30' y='214' class='svg-hand'>10:40 p.m.</text>\n<circle cx='205' cy='110' r='11' fill='#fff' stroke='#007a66' stroke-width='2.5'/><text x='172' y='86' class='svg-hand'>answer</text>\n<circle cx='330' cy='182' r='11' fill='#fff' stroke='#007a66' stroke-width='2.5'/><text x='298' y='222' class='svg-hand'>qualify</text>\n<circle cx='458' cy='104' r='11' fill='#fff' stroke='#c2410c' stroke-width='2.5'/><text x='412' y='80' class='svg-hand'>book viewing</text>\n<path d='M556 150 L590 122 L624 150 Z' fill='#e8f4f1' stroke='#007a66' stroke-width='2.5' stroke-linejoin='round'/>\n<rect x='562' y='150' width='56' height='44' rx='4' fill='#e8f4f1' stroke='#007a66' stroke-width='2.5'/>\n<rect x='583' y='168' width='14' height='26' rx='2' fill='#c2410c'/>\n<text x='622' y='222' text-anchor='end' class='svg-hand'>licensed agent</text>\n<rect x='24' y='16' width='370' height='26' rx='4' fill='#ffd8bf' opacity='0.7'/><text x='32' y='35' class='svg-t'>The AI opens the door. The agent walks them in.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Sketch 1.</b> The journey of one inquiry. The AI handles the first three stops in minutes; the licensed agent takes over at the door.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<div class='dd-myth'>\n<div class='dd-m'><span class='dd-lab'>Myth</span><p>An AI agent will replace the real estate agent.</p></div>\n<div class='dd-r'><span class='dd-lab'>Reality</span><p>Most buyers still buy through an agent. The AI removes the waiting and the repetitive questions so the agent arrives at a warmer conversation.</p></div>\n</div>\n<h2 id='qualify'>Which questions should an AI agent ask to qualify a buyer?</h2>\n<p class='dd-short'><b>Short answer:</b> four. Buy or rent, area and property type, budget range, and timeline. Add how they plan to pay once they show real interest.</p>\n<p>Every extra question costs you replies, so ask only what decides the next step. Offer the answers as quick-reply buttons where you can, and let the buyer skip a question. The full method for chat qualification is in <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/qualify-leads-messenger-automatically'>how to qualify leads in Messenger automatically</a>.</p>\n<div class='dd-code'><button class='dd-copy' type='button'>Copy</button><pre><code>Opener: Hi! Thanks for asking about [Listing name]. It's still available.\nI can share details or book a viewing. A few quick questions first?\n\n1. Are you looking to buy or rent?\n2. Which area and property type? (condo, house and lot, lot only)\n3. What budget range are you working with?\n4. When are you hoping to move? (this month, 1 to 3 months, later)\n\nIf timeline is this month or 1 to 3 months:\n“Great. Would you like to view it this week? Here are open slots: [slots]”\nAfter booking: “Booked. [Agent name], a licensed agent, will meet you there.”\n\nIf later: “No problem. Want me to send new listings that match?”</code></pre></div>\n<div class='dd-myth'>\n<div class='dd-m'><span class='dd-lab'>Myth</span><p>The more the bot asks up front, the more time the agent saves.</p></div>\n<div class='dd-r'><span class='dd-lab'>Reality</span><p>Long forms lose buyers. Four questions sort most leads, and some questions should never be asked at all (see the limits section below).</p></div>\n</div>\n<h2 id='speed'>How fast should a real estate lead get a reply?</h2>\n<p class='dd-short'><b>Short answer:</b> within minutes, every time, including nights and weekends.</p>\n<p>The research on online leads is consistent. The 2007 Lead Response Management Study by MIT's Dr. James Oldroyd and InsideSales.com found the odds of qualifying a lead were 21 times lower at 30 minutes than at 5 minutes. In a 2011 Harvard Business Review study of 2,241 US companies, firms that responded within an hour were nearly seven times as likely to qualify the lead as those that waited longer. Property inquiries arrive in the evening and on weekends, exactly when an office is closed. The evidence, and its limits, are in <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/lead-response-time'>lead response time: why the first five minutes matter</a>.</p>\n<h2 id='viewings'>How does an AI agent book viewings without double-booking?</h2>\n<p class='dd-short'><b>Short answer:</b> it reads and writes to the agent's real calendar, offers only open slots, and confirms and reminds automatically.</p>\n<p>Connect the agent to the calendar each licensed agent actually uses, set viewing length and travel buffer, and let the AI offer two or three slots instead of asking “when are you free?”. After booking, it sends a confirmation with the address and the agent's name, a reminder the day before and another two hours before, and a one-tap reschedule option. If a buyer calls instead of messaging, an <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/ai-voice-receptionist-appointments'>AI voice receptionist</a> can do the same on the phone line.</p>\n<figure class='dd-fig'>\n<svg viewBox='0 0 640 250' role='img' aria-labelledby='sc2t sc2d' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'>\n<title id='sc2t'>Two lanes: what the AI answers and what goes to a person</title>\n<desc id='sc2d'>A sketch with two lanes. The top lane, labelled AI agent, holds availability, price from listing, location, booking a viewing and reminders. The bottom lane, labelled licensed agent, holds value advice, offers and negotiation, paperwork and complaints. An orange arrow labelled hand off moves a message from the top lane to the bottom lane.</desc>\n<defs><pattern id='sc2g' width='16' height='16' patternUnits='userSpaceOnUse'><circle cx='2' cy='2' r='1' fill='#e6dccb'/></pattern></defs>\n<rect x='0' y='0' width='640' height='250' rx='14' fill='#fbf7f0'/>\n<rect x='0' y='0' width='640' height='250' rx='14' fill='url(#sc2g)'/>\n<text x='24' y='40' class='svg-hand'>AI agent</text>\n<line x1='24' y1='56' x2='616' y2='56' stroke='#007a66' stroke-width='2.5' stroke-dasharray='8 7' stroke-linecap='round'/>\n<rect x='24' y='68' width='112' height='34' rx='16' fill='#fff' stroke='#007a66' stroke-width='2'/><text x='38' y='90' class='svg-s'>availability</text>\n<rect x='146' y='68' width='112' height='34' rx='16' fill='#fff' stroke='#007a66' stroke-width='2'/><text x='164' y='90' class='svg-s'>listed price</text>\n<rect x='268' y='68' width='100' height='34' rx='16' fill='#fff' stroke='#007a66' stroke-width='2'/><text x='290' y='90' class='svg-s'>location</text>\n<rect x='378' y='68' width='122' height='34' rx='16' fill='#fff' stroke='#007a66' stroke-width='2'/><text x='392' y='90' class='svg-s'>book a viewing</text>\n<rect x='510' y='68' width='106' height='34' rx='16' fill='#fff' stroke='#007a66' stroke-width='2'/><text x='530' y='90' class='svg-s'>reminders</text>\n<path d='M300 112 C 300 140, 320 140, 320 162' fill='none' stroke='#c2410c' stroke-width='3' stroke-linecap='round'/>\n<path d='M312 152 L320 166 L328 152' fill='none' stroke='#c2410c' stroke-width='3' stroke-linecap='round' stroke-linejoin='round'/>\n<rect x='336' y='122' width='88' height='24' rx='4' fill='#ffd8bf' opacity='0.7'/><text x='344' y='140' class='svg-hand'>hand off</text>\n<text x='24' y='166' class='svg-hand'>licensed agent</text>\n<line x1='24' y1='180' x2='616' y2='180' stroke='#c2410c' stroke-width='2.5' stroke-dasharray='8 7' stroke-linecap='round'/>\n<rect x='24' y='192' width='128' height='34' rx='16' fill='#fff' stroke='#c2410c' stroke-width='2'/><text x='40' y='214' class='svg-s'>value advice</text>\n<rect x='162' y='192' width='168' height='34' rx='16' fill='#fff' stroke='#c2410c' stroke-width='2'/><text x='178' y='214' class='svg-s'>offers and negotiation</text>\n<rect x='340' y='192' width='122' height='34' rx='16' fill='#fff' stroke='#c2410c' stroke-width='2'/><text x='360' y='214' class='svg-s'>paperwork</text>\n<rect x='472' y='192' width='144' height='34' rx='16' fill='#fff' stroke='#c2410c' stroke-width='2'/><text x='490' y='214' class='svg-s'>complaints</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Sketch 2.</b> Two lanes. Facts from your listings stay with the AI; judgment, offers and anything sensitive move to a licensed agent.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h2 id='limits'>What must stay with a licensed agent?</h2>\n<p class='dd-short'><b>Short answer:</b> advice, offers, negotiation and paperwork, plus anything that touches fair housing, consent or a complaint.</p>\n<p>The rules differ by country, so check them with your own broker or lawyer. Three that matter for most readers:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Philippines.</b> Under the Real Estate Service Act (Republic Act No. 9646), no one may practice or offer real estate service without a license from the Professional Regulation Commission (Section 28). Keep the AI to listing facts and scheduling, and have a licensed broker or accredited salesperson handle advice and negotiation.</li>\n<li><b>United States, fair housing.</b> The Fair Housing Act still applies to every conversation. HUD withdrew its 2024 guidance on advertising through digital platforms in 2026, but the law itself did not change. The AI should never ask about or filter by protected traits such as race, religion, national origin, sex, disability or familial status, and should never steer a buyer toward or away from a neighborhood.</li>\n<li><b>United States, calls.</b> In February 2024 the FCC confirmed that AI-generated voices count as “artificial” voices under the Telephone Consumer Protection Act, so outbound AI voice calls need the person's prior express consent unless an exemption applies.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Personal data also needs care everywhere. For Philippine businesses, the consent steps are in <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/data-privacy-act-chatbots-philippines'>the Data Privacy Act guide for chatbots</a>. How to hand a conversation to a person cleanly is in <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/ai-chatbot-human-handoff'>the handoff playbook</a>.</p>\n<div class='dd-sticky'><span class='dd-note-label'>Dijae's rule</span><p>Let the AI open the door. Let a licensed agent walk the buyer through it.</p></div>\n<h2 id='try'>What can you set up today?</h2>\n<ol class='dd-try'>\n<li>Put every active listing in one knowledge file: price, location, size, availability, payment terms and viewing rules. Update it the day anything changes.</li>\n<li>Write the opener and the four qualifying questions above, in your own words.</li>\n<li>Connect each agent's calendar, with viewing length, travel buffer and two reminders.</li>\n<li>Write the handoff rule: price negotiation, financing questions, complaints and anything off-script go to a named licensed agent, with an alert.</li>\n<li>Add a nurture message for “later” buyers: new matching listings every two weeks, with an easy opt-out.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><b>How you will know it works</b></p>\n<div class='dd-table-wrap'><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Pass when</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Time to first reply</td><td>Under one minute, day and night</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Inquiry to booked viewing</td><td>Tracked weekly by listing and channel, and rising</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Viewing show rate</td><td>Tracked weekly; reminders sent for every booking</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Hot-lead handoff</td><td>A licensed agent replies within one hour in business hours</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Accuracy test</td><td>20 real past questions answered correctly from the listing file before launch</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Fair housing test</td><td>The agent declines to answer “is this a good area for [group]?” and hands off</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>An honest limitation: an AI agent is only as current as your listing data. If a unit is sold and the file is not updated, the agent will keep offering it, and that costs trust fast. It also cannot judge a property, read a buyer's hesitation during a viewing or give market advice. Budget time every week to update the listings and review conversations.</p>\n<h2 id='faq'>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Can an AI chatbot qualify real estate leads?</h3>\n<p>Yes. A chatbot or AI agent can ask a few qualifying questions, such as buy or rent, area, budget and timeline, then book a viewing or route the lead to a licensed agent. Keep the questions short and never ask about protected traits.</p>\n<h3>Will an AI agent replace real estate agents?</h3>\n<p>No. It handles first replies, scheduling and follow-up. NAR's 2025 survey found 88% of US buyers purchased through an agent or broker, and advice, negotiation and paperwork stay with licensed professionals.</p>\n<h3>Which channels should a real estate AI agent cover?</h3>\n<p>The ones your buyers already use. Look at where your inquiries come from today: Messenger, WhatsApp, website chat, text or phone. Start with the channel that brings the most inquiries.</p>\n<h3>Can an AI agent call leads for me?</h3>\n<p>It can, but in the US outbound calls with an AI-generated voice need the person's prior express consent under the Telephone Consumer Protection Act, unless an exemption applies. Answering inbound calls is the safer place to start.</p>\n<div class='dd-cta'>\n<p class='dd-cta-title'>Get an AI agent for your listings</p>\n<p>Want an AI agent that answers listing questions, qualifies buyers and books viewings for your team? <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/book'>Book a free AI Automation Blueprint call</a>. Tools that fit this well: <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/botcake' rel='sponsored nofollow'>Botcake</a> for Messenger and <a href='https://www.gohighlevel.com/?fp_ref=dijae-044b83' rel='sponsored nofollow'>GoHighLevel</a> for CRM pipelines and follow-up (affiliate links: I may earn a commission at no extra cost to you).</p>\n<p>Prefer to learn it step by step? <a href='https://grow.dijaedadula.com/newsletter'>Join the free weekly newsletter</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ol class='dd-refs'>\n<li><a href='https://www.nar.realtor/press-releases/first-time-home-buyer-share-falls-to-historic-low-of-21-median-age-rises-to-40' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>National Association of REALTORS®: 2025 Profile of Home Buyers and Sellers press release</a>, November 4, 2025 (6,103 responses, transactions July 2024 to June 2025).</li>\n<li><a href='https://www.mortech.com/hs-fs/hub/25649/file-13535879-pdf/docs/mit_study.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>The Lead Response Management Study</a>, Oldroyd (MIT Sloan) and Elkington (InsideSales.com), 2007.</li>\n<li><a href='https://hbr.org/2011/03/the-short-life-of-online-sales-leads' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Oldroyd, McElheran and Elkington: The Short Life of Online Sales Leads</a>, Harvard Business Review, March 2011.</li>\n<li><a href='https://batasnatin.com/laws/ra-9646' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Republic Act No. 9646, Real Estate Service Act of the Philippines</a> (2009), Sections 3 and 28.</li>\n<li><a href='https://www.jdsupra.com/legalnews/hud-withdraws-eight-fair-housing-8645237/' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>JD Supra: HUD withdraws eight fair housing guidance documents</a>, including the April 29, 2024 digital platforms advertising guidance.</li>\n<li><a href='https://cooley.com/news/insight/2024/2024-02-15-fcc-ai-generated-robocalls-illegal-under-the-tcpa' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Cooley: FCC rules AI-generated voices are “artificial” under the TCPA</a>, February 15, 2024.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2>\n<ul class='dd-more'>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/qualify-leads-messenger-automatically'>How to Qualify Leads in Messenger Automatically (Without Annoying Your Customers)</a></li>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/lead-response-time'>Lead Response Time: Why the First Five Minutes Decide Who Wins the Customer</a></li>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/ai-agent-instructions-template'>How to Write AI Agent Instructions for Any Business (Templates Inside)</a></li>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/blog'>See all posts on the blog</a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"height":8135,"left":160,"top":450,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"height":10782,"left":20,"top":388,"width":380}}}},{"id":"h_css2121","type":"html-box","specials":{"html":"&lt;style&gt;.dd-article ul{list-style:disc outside !important}.dd-article ol{list-style:decimal outside !important}.dd-article li{display:list-item !important}.dd-article ul ul{list-style:circle outside !important}&lt;/style&gt;"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"hei